WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:06.669
It was a beautiful day in Sardinia, the second-largest
Italian island in the Mediterranean.

00:00:06.669 --> 00:00:12.240
The sea was clear, the air was hot, and the
beaches were golden.

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:18.290
But the Cagliari Diving Club couldn’t see
any of that, they were roughly 250 meters

00:00:18.290 --> 00:00:21.140
underneath the mediterranean sea.

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:25.570
Given the rich and extensive history of the
area, they were sure to find some interesting

00:00:25.570 --> 00:00:28.760
historical artifacts on the ocean floor.

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:33.410
And they were indeed about to find something
incredible, but this history wasn’t quite

00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:36.790
as dead as some old Roman pottery.

00:00:36.790 --> 00:00:40.940
Paolo Bonacelli, the most experienced diver,
was the deepest of all.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:45.790
They’d decided to be a little more ambitious
this time than in previous dives - twenty

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:48.060
miles off the Sardinian coast.

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:53.810
For Paolo, it was uncharted territory, so
you could only imagine how amazed and delighted

00:00:53.810 --> 00:00:58.190
he was when he saw the shape of what seemed
like a small town beneath the water.

00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:04.440
Old, stone buildings in a classic Roman or
Grecian style, with roofs made of thatched

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:05.440
seaweed.

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:08.260
He gestured to his fellow divers to follow
him.

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:12.820
They were amazed at how well-preserved the
buildings seemed to be, as though they were

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:18.550
still being lived in and actively maintained
to this day, despite being around 300 meters

00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:19.550
underwater.

00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:23.810
If they were able to take some pictures and
collect some artifacts, they’d be the talk

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:29.220
of the local historic community, and probably
be able to finagle a payout from the whole

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:30.310
experience, too.

00:01:30.310 --> 00:01:36.869
That’s when Paolo spotted something truly
amazing: A larger, more impressive structure,

00:01:36.869 --> 00:01:42.880
like a miniature palace, surrounded by grandiose
statues of humanoid figures in a circle around

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:44.460
the little palace.

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:50.310
Each of the statues was an imposing five meters
tall, with a faint, golden light emanating

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:51.420
from each of them.

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:55.900
While the statues were humanoid, they definitely
weren’t human.

00:01:55.900 --> 00:02:01.590
Their features were strange and fish-like:
Scales, gills, tentacles.

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:03.439
Paolo was in awe at the sight of them.

00:02:03.439 --> 00:02:06.040
He took pictures and got closer.

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:10.569
There was also a huge chasm in front of the
building, perhaps some kind of underwater

00:02:10.569 --> 00:02:12.180
thermal vent.

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:15.530
Paolo was curious; he wanted to investigate
further.

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:17.560
He swam deeper and deeper.

00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:19.819
What was at the bottom of that chasm?

00:02:19.819 --> 00:02:24.760
But lucky for Paolo, he would never see what
was at the bottom of that chasm.

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:28.950
Before he could reach it, something intercepted
him from the side.

00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:30.760
Something large and fast.

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:35.590
He felt a white-hot flash of pain as claws
raked across his chest, tearing open the rubber

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:36.609
of his wetsuit.

00:02:36.609 --> 00:02:41.620
Paulo turned, eyes widening in horror, to
see a creature staring at him.

00:02:41.620 --> 00:02:45.060
Like the statues, it was humanoid but not
human.

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:51.519
An anthropomorphic sea monster with greenish
skin, its arms and legs coated in thin scales,

00:02:51.519 --> 00:02:53.900
its neck serrated into fleshy gills.

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:57.909
He could see scraps of his suit’s rubber
hanging from its claws.

00:02:57.909 --> 00:03:02.389
It bore a mouthful of fangs and gave a silent
but threatening snarl.

00:03:02.389 --> 00:03:07.500
Paolo could see something in the distance
behind this creature: More figures, like this

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:09.450
one, emerging from the murk.

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:10.959
Getting faster.

00:03:10.959 --> 00:03:12.829
Getting closer.

00:03:12.829 --> 00:03:18.349
Paolo was a smart man, but it didn’t take
a genius to realize that if he stuck around,

00:03:18.349 --> 00:03:23.260
something terrible was about to happen to
him and the rest of the Cagliari Diving Club.

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:28.010
He turned and fled, paddling with all his
might away from the coming legion of aquatic

00:03:28.010 --> 00:03:29.010
beasts.

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:33.200
The rest of the club saw the experienced diver
panicking and followed his lead.

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:37.560
Thanks to their quick thinking and expertise,
they all managed to escape with their lives

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:39.930
and only a few minor injuries.

00:03:39.930 --> 00:03:44.859
But they had no idea of the true extent of
the mystery they were leaving behind beneath

00:03:44.859 --> 00:03:45.949
the sea.

00:03:45.949 --> 00:03:48.459
The Multiverse is a big place.

00:03:48.459 --> 00:03:52.949
There are alternate universes where the Devourer
of Worlds escapes and destroys everything

00:03:52.949 --> 00:03:54.900
we love and hold dear.

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:59.609
There are alternate universes where the SCP
Foundation has gone haywire and attempted

00:03:59.609 --> 00:04:04.180
to wipe out humanity through controlled releases
of all of their anomalies.

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:09.439
There are even universes where a kill-squad
sent by the Chaos Insurgency hunts down and

00:04:09.439 --> 00:04:15.260
assassinates every member of the O5 Council,
before replacing them and leading the Foundation

00:04:15.260 --> 00:04:17.420
into a bold new era.

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:22.160
And there are some universes where the SCP
Foundation is Italian.

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:27.470
We’ve covered SCP-057 on this channel before
in our video on the most frightening rooms

00:04:27.470 --> 00:04:35.400
in the SCP universe, but you’ve never seen
this SCP-057, because this is the Italian

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:39.400
version: SCP-057-IT.

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:44.200
This localized anomaly off the coast of Sardinia
is under the purview of the Italian division

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:50.380
of the SCP Foundation, which works autonomously
with its own systems and terminology.

00:04:50.380 --> 00:04:55.660
This SCP isn’t a frightening room that crushes
its trapped victims together, this anomaly

00:04:55.660 --> 00:05:01.700
is an entire city 300 meters beneath the water
of the Mediterranean Sea.

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:06.820
Everyone has heard of the mythical lost city
of Atlantis, a supposed underwater utopia

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:11.770
outlined by such great historical minds as
the Ancient Greek philosopher Plato.

00:05:11.770 --> 00:05:17.510
It’s something that people fantasize about:
A beautiful, idyllic society under the sea,

00:05:17.510 --> 00:05:21.430
divorced from all the petty squabbles we deal
with up on land.

00:05:21.430 --> 00:05:23.940
But is everything really better down where
it’s wetter?

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:25.760
Let’s take a look and see.

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:30.060
When Paolo and the rest of the Cagliari Diving
Club returned to the surface, they were happy

00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:34.870
to tell anyone that would listen that they’d
encountered aggressive mermen and an entire

00:05:34.870 --> 00:05:37.670
underwater city off the coast of Sardinia.

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:42.640
They even posted their photos onto their official
Facebook page, along with photos of Paulo’s

00:05:42.640 --> 00:05:44.020
gnarly chest scars.

00:05:44.020 --> 00:05:49.120
That’s when the Italian branch of the SCP
Foundation finally discovered them and decided

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:50.120
to intervene.

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:54.710
The Foundation dispatched an SIR squad known
as Aureæ Notitiæ.

00:05:54.710 --> 00:06:00.950
SIRs are the Intelligence and Research Section
of the Italian SCP Foundation, a kind of Mobile

00:06:00.950 --> 00:06:05.100
Task Force that investigates possible informational
leads.

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:10.270
Paolo and his team were given amnestic treatment
and any evidence they’d collected was scrubbed

00:06:10.270 --> 00:06:11.590
from existence.

00:06:11.590 --> 00:06:18.080
Meanwhile, lieutenant Marco Levini, leader
of the Mobile Task Force SSM-II squad, aka

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:21.620
“Legio Atlantidis”
was being dispatched to the source of the

00:06:21.620 --> 00:06:26.200
problem, SCP-057-IT itself.

00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:31.070
What started off as a relatively straightforward
exploratory mission soon took an extremely

00:06:31.070 --> 00:06:32.810
strange turn.

00:06:32.810 --> 00:06:37.530
Levini and his men reported activity down
in the underwater city, observing from the

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:40.400
safety of their armored Foundation submarine.

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:46.530
While the aquatic humanoids living in 057-IT
were undeniably the same species, their culture

00:06:46.530 --> 00:06:51.639
seemed to be split up into two unique groups:
One group had thinner scales on their arms

00:06:51.639 --> 00:06:52.820
and legs.

00:06:52.820 --> 00:06:57.810
This group was more numerous, having at least
sixty active specimens, and was characterized

00:06:57.810 --> 00:07:01.310
by their extreme aggression towards any outsiders.

00:07:01.310 --> 00:07:06.010
As for the smaller group, they had thicker
scales, as well as a number of eerily consistent

00:07:06.010 --> 00:07:09.060
injuries to their hands, feet, and gills.

00:07:09.060 --> 00:07:14.370
They were also distinct from the thin-scales
in terms of behavior, as they were a far friendlier,

00:07:14.370 --> 00:07:15.650
more curious bunch.

00:07:15.650 --> 00:07:20.360
At times, members of this subset would approach
the submarine and regard it with detached

00:07:20.360 --> 00:07:21.360
fascination.

00:07:21.360 --> 00:07:25.570
Sometimes, they would even point at the submarine
and laugh, though their reasons for doing

00:07:25.570 --> 00:07:27.540
this are unknown.

00:07:27.540 --> 00:07:32.190
Eventually, Lieutenant Levini was so confident
in their safety around the merpeople that

00:07:32.190 --> 00:07:37.540
he and a few other team members decided to
disembark from the submarine on a diving excursion

00:07:37.540 --> 00:07:40.580
and properly explore the aquatic city below.

00:07:40.580 --> 00:07:44.760
This would prove to be a dangerous tactical
error on Levini’s part.

00:07:44.760 --> 00:07:49.280
During what seemed like a routine exploratory
mission, Levini was ambushed by a squadron

00:07:49.280 --> 00:07:52.500
of thin-scales, grabbed from behind, and kidnapped.

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:57.470
He was taken as a hostage and spirited away
into one of the city’s various buildings,

00:07:57.470 --> 00:08:00.800
where a thick-scale known as Laetitia acted
as his warden.

00:08:00.800 --> 00:08:05.820
But Levini soon found out that being under
Laetitia’s care was a profoundly lucky turn

00:08:05.820 --> 00:08:10.900
of events on his part, both because it allowed
him to learn more about the situation and

00:08:10.900 --> 00:08:15.419
because she was one of the small group left
in the city who hadn’t become dangerous

00:08:15.419 --> 00:08:16.419
fanatics.

00:08:16.419 --> 00:08:21.300
That’s right: The merpeople were in the
middle of a heated civil war.

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:25.540
Both from the observations of Levini during
his captivity, and later interviews conducted

00:08:25.540 --> 00:08:30.889
by project head Dr. Giuseppe Pistillo with
some liberated members of the thick-scales,

00:08:30.889 --> 00:08:37.279
they learned that a terrible religious conflict
had broken out in SCP-057-IT.

00:08:37.279 --> 00:08:41.759
The accounts coming from the rescued citizens
illustrated a similar backstory to what the

00:08:41.759 --> 00:08:47.120
Italian Foundation had theorized regarding
the merpeople: They were the descendants of

00:08:47.120 --> 00:08:53.140
peoples that lived on the island of Nisyros
up to the 14th century BCE before it was devastated

00:08:53.140 --> 00:08:58.629
by a volcanic eruption, forcing them into
the ocean, where they evolved the ability

00:08:58.629 --> 00:09:02.639
to live in aquatic environments through anomalous
means.

00:09:02.639 --> 00:09:08.010
Since this change, this new species has been
operating in Mediterranean waters, migrating

00:09:08.010 --> 00:09:13.820
regularly in order to avoid detection, passing
their way of life from generation to generation

00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:16.879
as the world changed and shifted above them.

00:09:16.879 --> 00:09:22.089
In many ways, they were quite similar to humans,
such as their reproductive habits - they mate

00:09:22.089 --> 00:09:27.730
and reproduce after a gestation period, more
like mammals than fish, though their gestation

00:09:27.730 --> 00:09:31.180
period is slightly shorter than human beings
at six months.

00:09:31.180 --> 00:09:36.990
They largely speak Latin, though the oldest
merperson among them also speaks Ancient Greek.

00:09:36.990 --> 00:09:42.249
Merchildren born in Foundation containment
have shown strong language acquisition skills,

00:09:42.249 --> 00:09:45.750
as they have proven more than able to learn
modern Italian.

00:09:45.750 --> 00:09:50.370
And even more fascinating from a standpoint
of sociological study, the merpeople have

00:09:50.370 --> 00:09:53.629
formed their own unique culture under the
sea.

00:09:53.629 --> 00:09:56.309
And this is where the problems started.

00:09:56.309 --> 00:10:00.870
Abstaining from the belief of the Greek and
Roman pantheons their ancestors looked up

00:10:00.870 --> 00:10:06.040
to, the merpeople instead worshipped their
own group of water-bound deities, whose images

00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:09.629
were reflected in the great statues in the
center of the town.

00:10:09.629 --> 00:10:14.420
The large building near the statues and the
chasm was the home of the “mayor”, the

00:10:14.420 --> 00:10:16.370
town’s de facto leader.

00:10:16.370 --> 00:10:21.350
However, what had been a workable system for
centuries began falling to ruin when a strange

00:10:21.350 --> 00:10:24.040
religious fanaticism began to spread.

00:10:24.040 --> 00:10:29.170
A cult-like group soon formed and began holding
ceremonies where they worshipped a powerful

00:10:29.170 --> 00:10:33.089
entity in the chasm known as The Great Eye.

00:10:33.089 --> 00:10:39.240
This new cult was known as the Cult of The
Great Eye of the Mediterranean, or CGEM for

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:40.240
short.

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:44.230
What began as a fringe belief soon became
a frenzy and took over the better part of

00:10:44.230 --> 00:10:48.670
the town, with the Acolytes of the Great Eye
proving themselves more than willing to spread

00:10:48.670 --> 00:10:51.860
the gospel of their new deity with violence.

00:10:51.860 --> 00:10:55.639
Some of the more ardent non-believers were
killed for their heresy, while others were

00:10:55.639 --> 00:11:00.019
simply ritualistically mutilated in order
to prevent them from rebelling.

00:11:00.019 --> 00:11:03.959
Laetitia had her own evidence of these targeted
mutilations.

00:11:03.959 --> 00:11:08.709
The thin-scales had cut the aquatic webbing
from between her fingers and toes, making

00:11:08.709 --> 00:11:11.860
it harder for her to swim away and escape.

00:11:11.860 --> 00:11:14.850
Other suspected heretics were given the same
treatment.

00:11:14.850 --> 00:11:19.270
The reason that the thick-scales even had
thicker scales was that they stole forbidden

00:11:19.270 --> 00:11:24.019
technology from the mayor to increase the
strength of their scales, hoping it would

00:11:24.019 --> 00:11:27.439
help them better withstand the torments of
the Acolytes.

00:11:27.439 --> 00:11:32.070
Those involved in the stealing of this technology
were captured and summarily executed for their

00:11:32.070 --> 00:11:33.089
acts of defiance.

00:11:33.089 --> 00:11:39.430
In a sense, Laetitia was protecting Levini
by advising him against trying to escape,

00:11:39.430 --> 00:11:43.110
knowing the Acolytes of the Great Eye would
kill him if he did.

00:11:43.110 --> 00:11:47.220
She knew that the only opportunity for escape
would come during the ceremony held by the

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:49.869
Acolytes to honor their frightening master.

00:11:49.869 --> 00:11:55.980
When the day eventually came, as Levini was
running low on everything from food to oxygen,

00:11:55.980 --> 00:12:00.060
everyone in the town was forced out into the
town center to witness the ritual.

00:12:00.060 --> 00:12:05.870
The Acolytes gathered around the chasm and
began to chant in a frightening, unknown language.

00:12:05.870 --> 00:12:11.130
As they chanted, a blinding light began to
emanate from the chasm, and as blurry shapes

00:12:11.130 --> 00:12:16.699
emerged, nightmarish, tentacled gastropods
soon began to take form.

00:12:16.699 --> 00:12:20.250
Truly Lovecraftian undersea monsters.

00:12:20.250 --> 00:12:24.670
Shortly after the ritual, Levini and the thick-scales
were able to make a break for it, pursued

00:12:24.670 --> 00:12:26.839
by the Acolytes of the Great Eye.

00:12:26.839 --> 00:12:31.139
It was a close one, but thankfully, due to
the intervention and assistance of a trained

00:12:31.139 --> 00:12:36.000
Mobile Task Force, the fanatical forces of
the Acolytes were repelled and the fleeing

00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:38.720
merpeople, along with Levini, were rescued.

00:12:38.720 --> 00:12:43.930
A number of thick-scales are now willingly
confined at Site Nettuno, an Italian Foundation

00:12:43.930 --> 00:12:48.770
containment site, where they have undergone
numerous interviews with Foundation staff.

00:12:48.770 --> 00:12:55.709
Incidentally, among them is the oldest merperson
previously present in SCP-057-IT, the only

00:12:55.709 --> 00:12:58.420
one who spoke Ancient Greek fluently.

00:12:58.420 --> 00:13:00.860
He was different from the others.

00:13:00.860 --> 00:13:01.860
Extremely different.

00:13:01.860 --> 00:13:07.500
In fact, he was a deity made into flesh, one
of the deities replaced by the worshippers

00:13:07.500 --> 00:13:09.290
of the Great Eye.

00:13:09.290 --> 00:13:14.839
This unfortunate former God had done everything
to keep his people’s lives safe and peaceful,

00:13:14.839 --> 00:13:20.329
but in spite of his wisdom and best efforts,
Hell had once again broken loose.

00:13:20.329 --> 00:13:25.370
Not everything is all well and good in SCP-057-IT.

00:13:25.370 --> 00:13:30.970
Even if a human’s body changes, their nature
does not, and the worst parts of human nature

00:13:30.970 --> 00:13:35.749
seemingly followed these unfortunate merpeople
into what should have been their paradise

00:13:35.749 --> 00:13:37.139
under the sea.

00:13:37.139 --> 00:13:39.079
But all hope isn’t lost.

00:13:39.079 --> 00:13:43.930
If you were to judge the entire human race
on one community in turmoil, you probably

00:13:43.930 --> 00:13:47.160
wouldn’t leave with a very favorable impression
of us, either.

00:13:47.160 --> 00:13:51.920
Correspondence with a French branch of the
SCP Foundation reveals that mercreatures aren’t

00:13:51.920 --> 00:13:55.850
just localized to one warring underwater city
in Sardinia.

00:13:55.850 --> 00:14:00.290
Mermaids have also been discovered and confirmed
by Foundation field agents off of the coast

00:14:00.290 --> 00:14:01.300
of France.

00:14:01.300 --> 00:14:05.529
Eighty percent of the Ocean still remains
unmapped to this day.

00:14:05.529 --> 00:14:09.980
Who knows what else is out there, just waiting
to be found?

00:14:09.980 --> 00:14:16.509
Now go check out “The Horror of Body Stealing
Rain - SCP-3300” and “SCP-1861 - The Crew

00:14:16.509 --> 00:14:20.939
of the HMS Wintersheimer” for more water-based
horrors from the SCP Foundation!

